# Deny everything, then allow only what the build needs.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . ./`, so an allowlist is the difference between "the build receives
# this directory's source" and "the build receives whatever a developer happens to have here" — a
# local appsettings.Development.json, a .env, or a certificate would otherwise land in a build
# layer. New .cs files are picked up automatically; anything else has to be allowed deliberately.
*
!*.cs
!*.csproj
